	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Terralith contributes dramatic terrain and many vanilla-block biomes. Biomes O' Plenty contributes additional biome families, plants and woods. TerraBlender helps biome providers participate in one world."
				"Serene Seasons then changes foliage colour, temperature and crop fertility through time. A biome looking different in a later visit may be seasonal change rather than a new generation bug."
				"Major terrain or structure discoveries require new chunks. Protect server performance by travelling with purpose instead of flying in several directions at maximum speed."
				"Serene Seasons changes colour, temperature, and crop fertility over time. Consult the season indicator and crop information before blaming a field layout that worked earlier in the year."
			]
			id: "18F17FA689C05B93"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2237B8AD7A576092"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Terrain shape, biome palette and season are different layers"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2CD80668B92F9030"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "How This Overworld Is Built"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["18F17FA689C05B93"]
			description: [
				"Nature's Compass searches registered biomes; Explorer's Compass searches registered structures. A missing result can mean the target is disabled, not registered, too distant or unavailable in existing chunks."
				"Search one destination at a time and write down the result before changing targets. The compass points toward a candidate; it does not promise an easy route or an untouched structure."
				"For ordinary palette hunting, explore naturally first. Save compass searches for a material, boss or project that genuinely needs a particular place."
				"Biome mods overlap by design: terrain shape, biome identity, foliage, animals, and ambient details can come from different projects. Use Jade, F3 biome information, and JEI rather than identifying only by colour."
			]
			id: "19C183EB737C11C0"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2EF03483FC54E29A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Biomes and structures are two different searches"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4E7A27EED5A04215"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Use the Right Compass"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["18F17FA689C05B93"]
			description: [
				"Serene Seasons divides spring, summer, autumn and winter into early, mid and late sub-seasons. With default timing that produces twelve visible phases rather than four instant switches."
				"Temperate regions show the full cycle, while tropical regions can behave more like wet and dry seasons. Snowy and very hot areas follow their climate instead of copying a plains biome."
				"Craft the seasonal calendar or use the season display available in the pack, then record planting dates. Planning is easier when the farm has a clock."
				"The Almanac of Turning Leaves asks settlements to adapt rather than erase seasons: diversified crops, preserved food, indoor work, planned expeditions, and festivals make environmental change part of play."
			]
			id: "2BA6DCD040FF394C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "75A9A72CACD0D7B6"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Early, mid and late phases make four seasons"
			tasks: [{
				id: "70C456E2CE7A14F5"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Twelve Parts of a Year"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2BA6DCD040FF394C"]
			description: [
				"Hover seeds and crops to see which seasons support them. In-season crops grow normally; out-of-season crops are much slower and consume more bonemeal for the same progress."
				"Group fields by season and label them. Maintain a small reserve of every seed so one missed harvest does not erase a crop until next year."
				"Use crop rotation as a reason to diversify meals. A server pantry is more resilient when it is not waiting on one summer ingredient."
				"Serene Seasons changes colour, temperature, and crop fertility over time. Consult the season indicator and crop information before blaming a field layout that worked earlier in the year."
			]
			id: "4F3635C500264A8B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "791357C448D9CBD3"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "The tooltip is a planting guide"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6794D388F5DA9F2C"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Read Seed Fertility"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4F3635C500264A8B"]
			description: [
				"Serene Seasons supports protected growing. Glass within roughly sixteen blocks above crops can provide greenhouse protection; sufficiently deep underground farms also escape ordinary surface seasons."
				"Bee pollination can help crops regardless of season. This makes a responsible apiary part of the food system rather than a separate resource factory."
				"Do not put every field underground just to defeat the mechanic. Keep seasonal outdoor farms for variety and reserve protected space for essential ingredients."
				"Protected growing can reduce seasonal disruption when configured conditions are met. Test a small greenhouse, compare it with an outdoor plot, and keep reserve seed before converting the entire food supply."
			]
			id: "0DB97AA1B4FFF13C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4C251483507E0EB3"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Three ways around the outdoor season"
			tasks: [{
				id: "37020D2DE05407A1"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Greenhouse, Cellar and Bees"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19C183EB737C11C0", "0DB97AA1B4FFF13C"]
			description: [
				"Biomes O' Plenty adds woods, flowers, grasses, stones and atmosphere across distinct biome families. Many of its best rewards are renewable building palettes rather than treasure chests."
				"Collect saplings and small samples, photograph the original biome and establish a nursery at home. Confirm sapling requirements before assuming every tree grows like oak."
				"A palette wall should record the biome name and coordinates. Materials become useful when builders know where they came from and how to renew them."
				"Bring renewable samples home, but keep wild populations and distinctive landscapes intact. A botanical garden should teach where plants came from instead of replacing the place that made them interesting."
			]
			id: "6A507C6B66A619AF"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0A0B21D41BFC58D2"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Bring saplings and cuttings home, not the whole landscape"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6E419539D991C347"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Biomes O' Plenty Is a Palette Library"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6A507C6B66A619AF"]
			description: [
				"Terralith uses vanilla blocks to create terrain with stronger silhouettes and biome transitions. Look across the land before choosing a road, base or railway grade."
				"Follow valleys, passes and rivers instead of flattening every obstacle. Distant Horizons is especially useful here because the shape of far terrain can guide a route without loading it all at full detail."
				"When a dramatic formation becomes a landmark, name it and preserve its outline. The terrain is part of the build palette."
				"Biome mods overlap by design: terrain shape, biome identity, foliage, animals, and ambient details can come from different projects. Use Jade, F3 biome information, and JEI rather than identifying only by colour."
			]
			id: "0049FA32C35487D9"
			rewards: [{
				id: "5821C2F5E1C90C5F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
