		{
			dependencies: ["5F4797613D215365"]
			description: [
				"Choose one biome near a travelled route and document its season, useful renewable materials, wildlife, hazards and a build palette that suits it."
				"Improve access without stripping the site: a marked trail, bridge, shelter or sample nursery is enough. Leave large trees and distinctive formations where they make the place recognisable."
				"The Chronicle names this work the Living Map. It remembers not only where a place is, but how explorers agreed to return without destroying it."
				"Bring renewable samples home, but keep wild populations and distinctive landscapes intact. A botanical garden should teach where plants came from instead of replacing the place that made them interesting."
